# Tracer: obtain the canonical reduced fraction of a rational
#
# Before (library-owned and trusted):
# import std basics
# by thm basics::rational_has_unique_reduced_fraction(q)
# Former behavior: the reusable name lived in std/basics and its existential
# conclusion was introduced by `trust`.
#
# Now (kernel-checked): the reserved bare theorem checks rational membership,
# constructs the canonical existential, verifies its well-definedness, and
# stores it. The existential is not an implicit direct builtin rule.

have q Q
by thm rational_has_unique_reduced_fraction(q)
obtain p, d from exist! p Z, d N+ st {q = p / d, gcd(p, d) = 1}
q = p / d
gcd(p, d) = 1

# Boundary: the call has arity one, requires a known `Q` argument, and cannot
# be module-qualified. Writing the fixed existential directly does not invoke
# this handler. Its conclusion uses an integer numerator, a positive-natural
# denominator, and gcd exactly 1.
# Evidence: target/release/litex -compact -isolated -runner -f examples/01_proof_patterns/rational_reduced_fraction_builtin_theorem.lit
